{
  "$comment": "Render mode and prerendered HTML bytes per route, from the CI mock-env build's prerender-manifest.json. Enforced by scripts/route-render-modes.mjs after the build in source-validation.yml (Exact-head Coverage) and ci.yml (Build + Layout). Entry: static | isr:<seconds> | param-prerender[:<seconds>] | dynamic, then html=<bytes> for a static or ISR page. A route may not lose cacheability, its HTML may not grow past recorded bytes plus max(5%, 4096 B), and a route with no entry fails closed. Written by `node apps/web/scripts/route-render-modes.mjs --next-dir apps/web/.next --write`, which adds, removes and tightens and never records a loss, or by `--admit-dynamic` / `--admit-from-log`, which inserts only a missing dynamic entry the check already named on an allowed prefix; an intended loss is a hand edit plus an unexpired overrides[route] entry (owner, reason, issue, removalCondition, evidence, expiresOn). First snapshot 2026-11-12 from main 0b82835e: 93 static, 2 isr, 19 param-prerender, 169 dynamic. The build must set CI=true like the workflows do: the /renders fixture routes are admitted only then, and they 404 as small static pages otherwise.",
  "schema": "jovie.route-render-modes/v1",
  "overrides": {
    "/[username]/tip/thank-you": {
      "owner": "@itstimwhite",
      "reason": "The payment return reads request headers and Checkout session search parameters, then verifies current paid status on the server for the matching recipient. Static or ISR rendering would not perform that verification on each return.",
      "issue": "JOV-12407",
      "removalCondition": "Remove if Checkout stops returning to this route or the request-specific server verification moves to an existing payment surface; reassess this runtime contract under JOV-12407 before expiry.",
      "evidence": "https://github.com/JovieInc/Jovie/actions/runs/43786968068/job/133036679060 records the measured dynamic build. apps/web/app/[username]/tip/thank-you/page.test.tsx verifies distinct request headers and pending-to-confirmed rechecks with a mocked verifier; real-payment production certification remains unclaimed.",
      "expiresOn": "2026-12-16"
    },
    "/product": {
      "owner": "@itstimwhite",
      "reason": "Main already prerenders /product at 87581 bytes against a recorded 83454 (45 bytes under the limit); this change adds about 500 bytes through one extra CSS chunk reference, with no views content on the page.",
      "issue": "JOV-14465",
      "removalCondition": "Remove once the /product drift on main is trimmed or accepted and the entry is re-baselined (JOV-14465).",
      "evidence": "https://github.com/JovieInc/Jovie/actions/runs/45005356258/job/137155650730 measured 88093 bytes; local mock-env builds measured base 86641c2e at 87581 bytes and this head at 88093 bytes.",
      "expiresOn": "2026-12-22"
    },
    "/v/[token]": {
      "owner": "@itstimwhite",
      "reason": "Shared dashboard views read the optional session on the server to choose between the signup card and the Save as dashboard button, so each visit renders on request, like the /p/[token] share link.",
      "issue": "JOV-14462",
      "removalCondition": "Remove once /v/[token] renders the view as ISR, revalidated on publish and revoke, with viewer state resolved on the client (JOV-14462).",
      "evidence": "https://github.com/JovieInc/Jovie/actions/runs/45005356258/job/137155650730 records the measured dynamic build for PR #26632.",
      "expiresOn": "2026-12-22"
    }
  },
